-- title:
--   Common branch value at a generic supersingular node
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and let `red : A →+* k` be a ring homomorphism. Let $a\in k$ lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$, and assume $a^{q^2}=a$, $a\ne 0$ and $a\ne 1728$. Let $f$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series. Assume: (i) $f$, as a Laurent series, is integral over `NodeLocalized.modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A.toSubring red a (a ^ q)`, the ring of series $g$ admitting $r,s\in A[X_0,X_1]$ with `pointEval A.toSubring red a (a ^ q) s ≠ 0` and $g\cdot\,$`modularEval`$\,s=\,$`modularEval`$\,r$, that is, the localisation at the point $(a,a^q)$ of the ring of polynomial expressions in the two modular generators; (ii) $f$ lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, i.e. $f=r/s$ with $r,s$ in the subring generated by the constants from $A$ together with `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of level $1\cdot q$ and with $s$ of nonzero reduction, and its image under the reduction homomorphism `modularRedLocHom` lies in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the subfield of $k$-Laurent series generated by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`; (iii) the same two conditions for the image of $f$ under `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-linear extension of the Fricke involution of that level. Then there is a single $c\in k$ such that the reduction of $f$ has value $c$ at the place `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a` and the reduction of the Fricke image of $f$ has value $c$ at the place `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k (a ^ q)`, where having value $c$ means the element lies in the valuation subring of the place and its residue is the image of $c$ in the residue field; these two places are the components of `frobNodePair q a`.
--
--   This is the generic case ($j\ne 0,1728$, $q\ge 5$) of the statement that, on the reduction modulo $q$ of the modular curve of level $q$, the two branches through a supersingular node — the $j$-line and its Frobenius twin, matched by the Fricke involution — assign the same value to any function integral over the local ring of the node. It feeds the unrestricted one-point statement [`ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_isIntegral_modularLocalizedAtPoint_of_pow_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_isIntegral_modularLocalizedAtPoint_of_pow_eq), from which the crossing of the two components of the mod-$q$ fibre at supersingular points is read off.
